  {
    "name": "the brake runs in a group on landing beside the blocking set, and a task that only starts with its name does not",
    "input": {
      "jobs": {
        "clippy": {
          "name": "check Clippy wall",
          "if": "${{ !cancelled() && github.base_ref != 'landing' }}",
          "steps": [
            {
              "run": "mise run check:clippy-plain-only"
            }
          ]
        },
        "brake": {
          "name": "hold the landings while main lags",
          "if": "${{ github.event_name == 'merge_group' && github.event.merge_group.base_ref == 'refs/heads/landing' }}",
          "steps": [
            {
              "run": "mise run ci:brake"
            }
          ]
        },
        "report": {
          "name": "report the brake",
          "if": "${{ github.event_name == 'merge_group' }}",
          "steps": [
            {
              "run": "mise run ci:brake-report"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "landing": ["check:clippy-plain-only"]
    },
    "output": [
      "`report` runs in a merge group on `landing` outside the blocking set: add `github.event.merge_group.base_ref != 'refs/heads/landing'` to its `if` (#5439)"
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "#6790: a join that saves the enforcing state on a push whose queue run holds none writes the state the nightly restores",
    "input": {
      "jobs": {
        "template": {
